+## Native admitted account identity
+
+The existing Provider writer may follow an external switch of a CLI's default login during
+discovery, allowance recovery or the next connection refresh. That creates a new model binding;
+it never changes an already admitted input. Default CLI homes and Fleet-owned homes obey the
+same execution-time account check. The former `followLogin` model flag must not bypass it.
+
+```text
+CLI login observation → Provider commit → new admitted model/account
+                                          → native identity check → request → account receipt
+```
+
+If the CLI's identity differs before dispatch, refuse before inference and tool effects, never
+resume a continuation under a different account, and use the existing connection recovery UI.
+Do not rewrite the CLI credentials, relabel an old request as a new account, or automatically
+replay a potentially accepted request. A later input can use the refreshed binding. Successful
+responses retain the account that was checked for that native request; unknown account state
+does not become an inferred identity. This correction adds no storage, configuration or login
+authority and requires no data migration. The native Codex/Claude integration fixtures use
+isolated homes and loopback providers to verify mismatch refusal and zero successful receipts.
+
